config CPU_ACCEL
	tristate "Single CPU accelerator prototype"
	depends on SMP
	depends on MMU
	help
	  Build the first experimental single-CPU accelerator control plane and
	  lifecycle backend.

	  The prototype exposes /dev/cpu_accel. A control process selects one
	  online CPU, maps a shared control and sample area, and starts a bounded
	  timestamp workload. During the workload the CPU remains online but has
	  preemption and local interrupts disabled. This is a development
	  experiment, not a production isolation mechanism or a hard latency
	  guarantee.
